TASK 5 – THREE GREEDY ENGINEERS, ONE NETWORK
Kruskal’s Algorithm, Prim’s Algorithm and Borůvka’s Algorithm
1. Aim
To implement Kruskal’s, Prim’s and Borůvka’s algorithms using the same connected weighted graph, find the Minimum Spanning Tree (MST), display the edge-selection sequence, and compare their behaviour in different deployment environments.
2. Graph used
Consider a company with six facilities: A, B, C, D, E and F. The edges represent possible network connections, and their weights represent installation costs.

Base graph – 6 vertices and 9 weighted edges
Edge	Cost
A–B	4
